-- Version: 6.9.0 -- ROLLBACK to the 6.8.0 line + food hand-out fix
--
-- Base is v6.8.0 (seat only ^T%d+$, tray pickup with no text filter, token bucket
-- 8 calls / 0.5 s, ClassName-only part lookup, no task.wait inside collection).
-- v7.x and v8.0.0 are discarded: the user's baseline is 6.8.0.
--
-- ONLY the SERVE path changed from 6.8.0:
-- BUG: oneServe() read foodList(ty) BEFORE pickupViaPrompt(), then handed out those
-- pre-pickup models. The tray grab replaces what is on the counter, so the models being
-- served were stale. FIX: pickup -> task.wait(0.15) settle -> re-read foodList -> serve.
-- Also: one dish at a time with a 0.12 s gap (a burst of 5 in one frame was dropped), and a
-- dish that fails twice is skipped for 8 s so one bad model cannot stall the loop.
--
-- Call shapes unchanged (confirmed, differ - never assume uniformity):
--   bill  = Interacted THEN TaskCompleted 'CollectBill'   (2)
--   dish  = TaskCompleted 'CollectDishes'                 (1)
--   tips  = TipsCollected                                 (1)
--   order = TaskCompleted 'TakeOrder'                     (1)
--   seat  = TaskCompleted 'SendToTable'                   (1)
--   serve = fireproximityprompt (tray) then TaskCompleted 'Serve' per dish
--
-- Loader:
-- loadstring(game:HttpGet("https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bobashid/roblox-matcha/refs/heads/main/Restaurant%20Tycoon%203?v=" .. tostring(os.time()), true))()

